  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: No experiments have been completed, so we have no baseline for either modality. The central question in a multimodal cellular profiling study is whether combining modalities improves over the best single modality, but this cannot be assessed without knowing how well each modality performs alone. 2) What this tests: config_028 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the simplest possible image-only model—no aggregation, no fusion, a well-understood pretrained encoder. It establishes the performance floor for the image modality and confirms that the pipeline works end-to-end with minimal confounds. 3) Why it is the best first experiment: Under a limited budget, a clean unimodal baseline is the highest-information first step because (a) it is fast and has few failure modes, (b) it provides the reference needed to interpret every subsequent multimodal result (e.g., config_001, 009, 019), (c) it isolates the image encoder and single-profile setting so that later experiments can cleanly attribute gains to added modalities, multiprofile aggregation, or fusion strategy, and (d) if it already performs strongly, it immediately reshapes the search toward understanding whether RNA adds value rather than wasting budget on multimodal variants that may not help."
